From: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject.toml: Relax build requirements

Lower the setuptools and setuptools-scm minimum versions to match the
versions provided by Scarthgap (setuptools 69.1.1, setuptools-scm 8.0.4).
The version is read from lark.__version__ (dynamic attr) and there is no
tool.setuptools_scm section, so the newer versions are not needed.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5-5
AI-Generated: Uses Claude (claude-sonnet-5-5)
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
---
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 [build-system]
-requires = ["setuptools>=80", "setuptools-scm>=9.2.2"]
+requires = ["setuptools>=69.1.1", "setuptools-scm>=8.0.4"]
 build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"
 
 [project]
